# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# catalog-admin build context
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# `.env` is excluded and its exclusion is load-bearing. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable
# it can see into the JavaScript it ships to the browser, so the host's `.env` — which
# points at http://localhost:4000 — must not reach the build. The Docker configuration
# arrives as explicit build args instead (VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api).
#
# What must NOT be listed here:
#   package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml   the frozen install
#   pnpm-workspace.yaml            pnpm settings (allowBuilds: esbuild)
#   index.html                     Vite's entry document
#   tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts  the type-checked build and the `@` alias
#   src/                           including src/fonts/*.woff2, referenced from src/index.css
#   nginx.conf                     copied into the final stage
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Host dependency tree and host build output.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Host environment — see the note above; this one matters more than usual.
.env
.env.*

# Tests, coverage and lint config. `pnpm build` runs `tsc --noEmit && vite build`, neither
# of which reads these (tsconfig.json covers src/ for the build).
tests/
coverage/
vitest.config.ts
vitest.setup.ts
eslint.config.mjs

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Documentation and Docker artefacts that no runtime code reads.
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Logs and scratch files.
*.log
*.tmp
